<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>NIS2 evidence report · {{ d.target }}</title>
{#- The report is one self-contained file: no scripts, fonts or images from elsewhere.
    Every chart below is plain HTML drawn from the scan data. #}
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f5f6f4; --card: #ffffff; --fg: #1a2130; --muted: #5d6573; --faint: #7c8391;
    --line: #dde0e4; --accent: #2f4b8a;
    --crit: #7a1712; --crit-bg: #f6d9d6;
    --red: #b3261e; --red-bg: #fbe9e7; --red-dot: #cf3a2f;
    --amber: #8a5a00; --amber-bg: #fdf1d6; --amber-dot: #d99a1e;
    --green: #1e6b3a; --green-bg: #e3f2e7; --green-dot: #2f8f52;
    --grey: #5d6573; --grey-bg: #eceef0; --grey-dot: #cfd3d9;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #12151b; --card: #1a1e26; --fg: #e8eaee; --muted: #a2a9b5; --faint: #858c99;
      --line: #2c323d; --accent: #9db4ff;
      --crit: #ffb4ab; --crit-bg: #4a1714;
      --red: #ff8a80; --red-bg: #3a1c19; --red-dot: #e0584d;
      --amber: #ffcc66; --amber-bg: #3a2e12; --amber-dot: #c98f1c;
      --green: #7fd69a; --green-bg: #173222; --green-dot: #3fa665;
      --grey: #a2a9b5; --grey-bg: #262b34; --grey-dot: #3b424e;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg);
         font: 15px/1.55 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 20px 72px; display: grid; gap: 44px; }
  h1, h2, h3 { margin: 0; text-wrap: balance; }
  h1 { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.01em; line-height: 1.2; }
  h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; }
  h3 { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.35; }
  p { margin: 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  code, .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .small { font-size: 13px; }
  section { display: grid; gap: 16px; min-width: 0; }
  .sec-head { display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .label { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }

  .masthead { display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 16px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .meta b { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .disclaimer { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 75ch; }

  .panel { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; display: grid; gap: 24px; }
  .headline { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.35; max-width: 40ch; }
  .headline em { font-style: normal; color: var(--red); }
  .headline .ok { color: var(--green); }
  .headline small { display: block; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .glance { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 1fr; gap: 28px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .glance { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .glance .label { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .units { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; }
  .u { width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--grey-dot); }
  .ns { background: var(--red-dot); }
  .ev { background: var(--green-dot); }
  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 18px; margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13px; }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .legend i { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 3px; display: inline-block; }
  .legend b { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .sev-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 8px; }
  .sev { border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 12px; display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .sev b { font-size: 28px; line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 800; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .sev span { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; }
  .sev-bar { display: flex; height: 8px; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; margin-top: 12px; gap: 2px; background: var(--grey-bg); }
  .checks-line { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13.5px; }

  .critical { background: var(--crit-bg); color: var(--crit); }
  .high, .not_satisfied, .fail { background: var(--red-bg); color: var(--red); }
  .medium, .error { background: var(--amber-bg); color: var(--amber); }
  .low, .not_assessed, .not_applicable { background: var(--grey-bg); color: var(--grey); }
  .evidenced, .partially_evidenced, .pass { background: var(--green-bg); color: var(--green); }
  .pill { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 9px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
  .cap { text-transform: capitalize; }

  .fix-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
  .fix-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr 150px; gap: 14px; align-items: center; padding: 12px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .fix-list li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .fix-list li > .pill { justify-self: start; }
  .fix-list a { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .fix-list a:hover, .fix-list a:focus-visible { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .fix-list .what { display: grid; gap: 1px; min-width: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .fix-list li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; } }
  .effort { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .effort i { display: inline-flex; gap: 2px; }
  .effort s { width: 6px; height: 12px; border-radius: 1px; background: var(--grey-dot); }
  .effort s.on { background: var(--accent); }

  .map { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .measure { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; display: grid; gap: 10px; align-content: start; }
  .measure.bad { border-color: var(--red-dot); }
  .measure-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; }
  .ico { width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; display: grid; place-items: center; flex: none; }
  .ico svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.8; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .measure h3 { font-size: 15px; }
  .art { font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); }
  .dots { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 3px; }
  .dots i { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--grey-dot); }
  .dots i.ns { background: var(--red-dot); }
  .dots i.ev { background: var(--green-dot); }
  .detail { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .detail b { color: var(--red); white-space: nowrap; }

  .gap { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6px 1fr; }
  .stripe.critical { background: var(--crit); }
  .stripe.high { background: var(--red-dot); }
  .stripe.medium { background: var(--amber-dot); }
  .stripe.low { background: var(--grey-dot); }
  .gap-body { padding: 18px 20px; display: grid; gap: 14px; min-width: 0; }
  .gap-head { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .gap-head .row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; align-items: center; }
  .compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .cmp { border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 12px; display: grid; gap: 2px; align-content: start; }
  .cmp .k { font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .cmp.found { background: var(--red-bg); }
  .cmp.found .k { color: var(--red); }
  .cmp.should { background: var(--green-bg); }
  .cmp.should .k { color: var(--green); }
  .cmp p { font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .why { max-width: 75ch; }
  .todo { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .todo .row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 12px; align-items: center; }
  .todo ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .ai { font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); }
  .gap details { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 10px; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 600; }
  summary:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 3px; }
  .legal { display: grid; gap: 12px; margin-top: 10px; }
  blockquote { margin: 4px 0 0; padding: 4px 12px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .kv { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 2px 12px; font-size: 13px; margin: 0; }
  .kv dt { color: var(--muted); }
  .kv dd { margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

  .narrative { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 16px; display: grid; gap: 8px; max-width: 80ch; }
  .note { background: var(--grey-bg); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 14px; }

  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em; }

  .terms { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 6px 16px; font-size: 14px; margin: 0; }
  .terms dt { font-weight: 600; }
  .terms dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  ul.method { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 6px; max-width: 80ch; }
  footer { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }

  @media print {
    :root { color-scheme: light; }
    body { background: #fff; }
    main { gap: 28px; }
    .panel, .gap, .measure, .fix-list li { break-inside: avoid; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{%- set ICONS = {
  "policy": '<path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 4.5-3.4 8.3-8 9-4.6-.7-8-4.5-8-9V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/>',
  "incident": '<path d="M12 3L2 20h20z"/><path d="M12 10v4M12 17h.01"/>',
  "backup": '<ellipse cx="12" cy="6" rx="7" ry="3"/><path d="M5 6v6c0 1.7 3.1 3 7 3s7-1.3 7-3V6M5 12v6c0 1.7 3.1 3 7 3s7-1.3 7-3v-6"/>',
  "supply": '<path d="M10 14a4 4 0 0 0 5.7 0l3-3a4 4 0 0 0-5.7-5.7l-1 1"/><path d="M14 10a4 4 0 0 0-5.7 0l-3 3a4 4 0 0 0 5.7 5.7l1-1"/>',
  "code": '<path d="M8 8l-4 4 4 4M16 8l4 4-4 4M13 5l-2 14"/>',
  "gauge": '<path d="M4 16a8 8 0 1 1 16 0"/><path d="M12 16l4-5"/>',
  "training": '<path d="M2 9l10-5 10 5-10 5z"/><path d="M6 11v5c3 2 9 2 12 0v-5"/>',
  "lock": '<rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/>',
  "access": '<circle cx="9" cy="8" r="4"/><path d="M2 21c0-4 3-6 7-6s7 2 7 6M17 11l2 2 3-3"/>',
  "mfa": '<rect x="7" y="2" width="10" height="20" rx="2"/><path d="M11 18h2M10 8h4v4h-4z"/>',
  "report": '<path d="M4 4h16v12H8l-4 4z"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 12h5"/>',
} %}
{%- set EFFORT = {
  "quick": ("Quick fix", 1, "A setting, a password or a line of configuration"),
  "change": ("Needs a change", 2, "A configuration or process change that needs some testing"),
  "project": ("Project", 3, "Planned work, such as upgrading several systems"),
} %}
{%- set STATUS = {
  "not_satisfied": "Problems found",
  "partially_evidenced": "Evidence found",
  "evidenced": "Evidenced",
  "not_assessed": "Not checked",
} %}
{%- macro effort(level) -%}
  {%- set label, bars, hint = EFFORT[level] -%}
  <span class="effort" title="{{ hint }}"><i>{% for n in range(3) %}<s class="{{ 'on' if n < bars }}"></s>{% endfor %}</i>{{ label }}</span>
{%- endmacro %}
{%- set total_checks = d.findings|length %}
{%- set fails = d.check_counts.fail %}
{%- set errors = d.check_counts.error %}
{%- set n_req = d.verdict_counts.values()|sum %}
{%- set n_ev = d.verdict_counts.partially_evidenced + d.verdict_counts.evidenced %}
{%- set sev_counts = {} %}
{%- for s in ["critical", "high", "medium", "low"] %}{% set _ = sev_counts.update({s: d.gaps|selectattr("severity", "equalto", s)|list|length}) %}{% endfor %}
{%- set urgent = d.gaps|selectattr("severity", "in", ["critical", "high"])|list or d.gaps[:3] %}
<main>
  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="label">NIS2 evidence report</div>
    <h1>{{ d.target }}</h1>
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Scanned <b>{{ d.started_at[:16].replace("T", " ") }} UTC</b></span>
      <span>{{ d.tool }}</span>
      <span>Profile <span class="mono">{{ d.profile_sha256[:12] }}</span></span>
    </div>
    <p class="disclaimer">
      This report sets out technical evidence collected from the target and judged by
      automated, deterministic checks. It is <b>not</b> a statement of NIS2 compliance. Much of
      NIS2 is organisational and needs an audit, so requirements the tool cannot check are
      shown as <i>not checked</i>, never as passed.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="glance">
    <h2 id="glance" hidden>At a glance</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="headline">
        {%- if fails == 0 and errors == 0 %}
        <span class="ok">All {{ total_checks }} checks passed.</span>
        <small>They give partial evidence for {{ n_ev }} of {{ n_req }} legal requirements. The other {{ d.verdict_counts.not_assessed }} need other evidence, such as an audit.</small>
        {%- else %}
        {%- if fails == total_checks %}<em>All {{ total_checks }} checks failed.</em>{% elif fails %}<em>{{ fails }} of {{ total_checks }} checks failed.</em>{% else %}No check failed.{% endif %}
        {%- if sev_counts.critical %} {{ sev_counts.critical }} {{ "problem is" if sev_counts.critical == 1 else "problems are" }} critical{% if sev_counts.high %} and {{ sev_counts.high }} {{ "is" if sev_counts.high == 1 else "are" }} high severity{% endif %}.
        {%- elif sev_counts.high %} {{ sev_counts.high }} {{ "problem is" if sev_counts.high == 1 else "problems are" }} high severity.{% endif %}
        {%- if errors %} {{ errors }} {{ "check" if errors == 1 else "checks" }} could not run.{% endif %}
        {%- endif %}
      </p>
      <div class="glance">
        <div>
          <div class="label">{{ n_req }} legal requirements · one square each</div>
          <div class="units" role="img" aria-label="{{ d.verdict_counts.not_satisfied }} not satisfied, {{ n_ev }} with evidence, {{ d.verdict_counts.not_assessed }} not checked">
            {%- for _ in range(d.verdict_counts.not_satisfied) %}<i class="u ns"></i>{% endfor %}
            {%- for _ in range(n_ev) %}<i class="u ev"></i>{% endfor %}
            {%- for _ in range(d.verdict_counts.not_assessed) %}<i class="u"></i>{% endfor -%}
          </div>
          <div class="legend">
            <span><i class="ns"></i><b>{{ d.verdict_counts.not_satisfied }}</b> not satisfied</span>
            <span><i class="ev"></i><b>{{ n_ev }}</b> partially evidenced</span>
            <span><i style="background:var(--grey-dot)"></i><b>{{ d.verdict_counts.not_assessed }}</b> not checked by this tool</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="label">Problems found, by severity</div>
          {%- if not d.gaps %}
          <p class="headline" style="font-size:18px">No problems found.</p>
          {%- else %}
          <div class="sev-row">
            {%- for s in ["critical", "high", "medium", "low"] %}
            <div class="sev {{ s }}"><b>{{ sev_counts[s] }}</b><span class="cap">{{ s }}</span></div>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
          <div class="sev-bar" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for s, colour in [("critical", "--crit"), ("high", "--red-dot"), ("medium", "--amber-dot"), ("low", "--grey-dot")] %}
            {%- if sev_counts[s] %}<div style="flex:{{ sev_counts[s] }};background:var({{ colour }})"></div>{% endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
          <p class="checks-line muted">{{ fails }} of {{ total_checks }} checks failed · {{ d.check_counts.pass }} passed{% if errors %} · {{ errors }} could not run{% endif %}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if narrative and narrative.status == "accepted" %}
  <section>
    <h2>Executive summary</h2>
    <div class="narrative">
      <p>{{ narrative.narrative.executive_summary }}</p>
      <p class="ai">
        Drafted by {{ narrative.model }} from the findings in this report only. Every cited
        finding, every number and full gap coverage were verified mechanically
        (attempt {{ narrative.attempts }}). Sources: {{ narrative.narrative.executive_summary_finding_ids|join(", ") }}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% elif narrative %}
  <div class="note">
    An AI-drafted narrative was generated but <b>rejected</b> by the validator, so it is not
    shown. Reasons: {{ narrative.violations|join("; ") }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if d.gaps %}
  <section aria-labelledby="fix-first">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="fix-first">Fix these first</h2>
      <p class="muted small">
        {%- if urgent[0].severity in ["critical", "high"] %}The critical and high-severity problems, most urgent first.{% else %}The most severe problems found.{% endif %}
        Each links to its details below.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="fix-list">
      {%- for g in urgent %}
      <li>
        <span class="pill cap {{ g.severity }}">{{ g.severity }}</span>
        <div class="what"><a href="#{{ g.finding_id }}">{{ g.action }}</a><span class="muted small">{{ g.found or g.message }}</span></div>
        {{ effort(g.effort) }}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section aria-labelledby="measures">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="measures">The NIS2 security measures</h2>
      <p class="muted small">Article 21(2) lists ten measures every organisation must take, and Article 23(4)
        adds incident reporting. Each small square is one detailed requirement from Implementing
        Regulation (EU) 2024/2690.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="map">
      {%- for a in d.articles %}
      {%- set ok = a.detailed_assessed - a.detailed_not_satisfied %}
      <div class="measure{{ ' bad' if a.verdict == 'not_satisfied' }}">
        <div class="measure-top">
          <div class="ico {{ a.verdict }}"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">{{ ICONS[a.icon]|safe }}</svg></div>
          <span class="pill {{ a.verdict }}">{{ STATUS[a.verdict] }}</span>
        </div>
        <div><h3>{{ a.short_title }}</h3><div class="art">Art. {{ a.point }}</div></div>
        {%- if a.detailed %}
        <div class="dots" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- for _ in range(a.detailed_not_satisfied) %}<i class="ns"></i>{% endfor %}
          {%- for _ in range(ok) %}<i class="ev"></i>{% endfor %}
          {%- for _ in range(a.detailed - a.detailed_assessed) %}<i></i>{% endfor -%}
        </div>
        <div class="detail">{{ a.detailed }} detailed requirements
          {%- if not a.detailed_assessed %}, none checked yet
          {%- else %}:
          {%- if a.detailed_not_satisfied %} <b>{{ a.detailed_not_satisfied }} failing</b>{% if ok or a.detailed > a.detailed_assessed %} ·{% endif %}{% endif %}
          {%- if ok %} {{ ok }} with evidence{% if a.detailed > a.detailed_assessed %} ·{% endif %}{% endif %}
          {%- if a.detailed > a.detailed_assessed %} {{ a.detailed - a.detailed_assessed }} not checked{% endif %}
          {%- endif %}</div>
        {%- else %}
        <div class="detail">No detailed requirements in the catalog yet</div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="gaps">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="gaps">Problems to fix ({{ d.gaps|length }})</h2>
      <p class="muted small">One entry per failing check, most severe first.</p>
    </div>
    {% if not d.gaps %}<p>No check failed.</p>{% endif %}
    {% for g in d.gaps %}
    {% set story = explanations.get(g.finding_id) %}
    <article class="gap" id="{{ g.finding_id }}">
      <div class="stripe {{ g.severity }}"></div>
      <div class="gap-body">
        <div class="gap-head">
          <div class="row"><span class="pill cap {{ g.severity }}">{{ g.severity }}</span>{% if g.topic %}<span class="muted small">{{ g.topic }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
          <h3>{{ g.message }}</h3>
        </div>
        {% if g.found %}
        <div class="compare">
          <div class="cmp found"><span class="k">Found</span><p>{{ g.found }}</p></div>
          <div class="cmp should"><span class="k">Should be</span><p>{{ g.should }}</p></div>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        <p class="why">{{ story.why_it_matters if story else g.why }}</p>
        <div class="todo">
          <div class="row"><span class="label">What to do</span>{{ effort(g.effort) }}</div>
          {% if story %}
          <ol>{% for step in story.remediation %}<li>{{ step }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>
          <p class="ai">Explanation and steps drafted by AI from this finding only; cites {{ story.requirement_ids|join(", ") }}; verified mechanically.</p>
          {% else %}
          <p>{{ g.action }}.</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        <details>
          <summary>Evidence and legal basis ({{ g.breaches|length }} requirement{{ "s" if g.breaches|length != 1 }} not satisfied)</summary>
          <div class="legal">
            <dl class="kv">
              <dt>Check</dt><dd><span class="mono">{{ g.finding_id }}</span> · {{ g.title }}</dd>
              <dt>Observed</dt><dd class="mono">{{ g.observed|tojson }}</dd>
              <dt>Expected</dt><dd class="mono">{{ g.expected|tojson }}</dd>
              <dt>Evidence</dt><dd class="mono">{{ g.evidence_ref }}{% if g.evidence_sha256 %} (sha256 {{ g.evidence_sha256[:16] }}…){% endif %}</dd>
            </dl>
            {% for b in g.breaches %}
            <div>
              <span class="mono">{{ b.requirement_id }}</span> · {{ b.title }}
              <div class="muted small">{{ b.provision }} · NIS2 Art. {{ b.nis2_article }}</div>
              <blockquote>“{{ b.quote }}”</blockquote>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="all-checks">
    <h2 id="all-checks">All checks</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Check</th><th>Status</th><th>Severity</th><th>Result</th></tr>
      {% for f in d.findings %}
      <tr>
        <td><span class="mono">{{ f.check_id }}</span><br>{{ f.title }}</td>
        <td><span class="pill {{ f.status }}">{{ f.status.replace("_", " ") }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="pill {{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity }}</span></td>
        <td>{{ f.message }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="assessed">
    <h2 id="assessed">Checked requirements ({{ d.verdicts|length }})</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Provision</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
      {% for v in d.verdicts %}
      <tr>
        <td><span class="mono">{{ v.requirement_id }}</span><br>{{ v.title }}</td>
        <td>{{ v.provision }}</td>
        <td><span class="pill {{ v.verdict }}">{{ v.verdict.replace("_", " ") }}</span></td>
        <td>{{ v.reason }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table></div>
    <details>
      <summary>Not checked by this tool ({{ d.not_assessed|length }} requirements)</summary>
      <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top:10px"><table>
        <tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Provision</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
        {% for v in d.not_assessed %}
        <tr><td><span class="mono">{{ v.requirement_id }}</span><br>{{ v.title }}</td><td>{{ v.provision }}</td><td>{{ v.reason }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table></div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="terms">
    <h2 id="terms">Terms used in this report</h2>
    <dl class="terms">
      <dt>NIS2</dt><dd>Directive (EU) 2022/2555, the EU law on cybersecurity for essential and important entities.</dd>
      <dt>CIR 2024/2690</dt><dd>Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2690, which sets out NIS2's technical measures in detail for digital service providers.</dd>
      <dt>CSIRT</dt><dd>Computer Security Incident Response Team: the national body that significant incidents are reported to.</dd>
      <dt>MFA, two-factor login</dt><dd>A second proof of identity beyond the password, such as a code from a phone app.</dd>
      <dt>TLS, HTTPS</dt><dd>The encryption that protects traffic to a website. Older TLS versions have known weaknesses.</dd>
      <dt>SSH</dt><dd>The remote login used by administrators to manage servers.</dd>
      <dt>CVE</dt><dd>A publicly known software flaw with a catalogue number.</dd>
      <dt>Partially evidenced</dt><dd>A check passed, but it covers only part of what the requirement asks for.</dd>
      <dt>Not checked</dt><dd>No automated check covers the requirement. It needs other evidence, such as an audit.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="method">
    <h2 id="method">Method and limits</h2>
    <ul class="method">
      <li>Every verdict comes from deterministic, unit-tested checks. No language model is involved in any pass/fail decision.</li>
      <li>Requirements are either hand-authored from NIS2 or extracted from CIR 2024/2690 by an LLM. Each one carries a verbatim quote that was verified against the official text and approved by a human reviewer.</li>
      <li>Each check covers only part of the obligations it maps to, so the best possible verdict is <i>partially evidenced</i>.</li>
      <li>Thresholds (log retention, backup age, password length and so on) come from the organisation's own profile, not from the law, which leaves them open.</li>
      <li>Severity, effort, the actions and the "found / should be" lines are written by hand for each check and filled in from the scan's own values.</li>
      {% if narrative and narrative.status == "accepted" %}<li>Narrative text is AI-drafted from this report's findings. It was accepted only after a validator confirmed that every gap is covered, every citation refers to a real failing finding, and no number or standard appears that is not in the data.</li>{% endif %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer>Generated by nis2scan. Raw evidence is in the <code>evidence/</code> directory next to this report.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
